{"seq":4,"slug":"computation","title":"计算哲学：信息、计算与数字存在","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-information/computation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"philosophy-of-computation","title":"计算哲学：Church-Turing 论题的边界","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-information/computation/philosophy-of-computation","wordCount":604,"readingTime":3},{"seq":2,"slug":"information-dynamics","title":"信息动力学：信道理论与信息流","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-information/computation/information-dynamics","wordCount":707,"readingTime":3},{"seq":3,"slug":"digital-ontology","title":"数字本体论：信息结构主义与存在的信息基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/philosophy-of-information/computation/digital-ontology","wordCount":728,"readingTime":3}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"计算哲学-信息-计算与数字存在\">计算哲学：信息、计算与数字存在</h1><p>本章探讨计算与信息的深层本质问题：Church-Turing 论题的哲学含义、信息流的形式理论、以及数字本体论对&quot;现实是什么&quot;的根本性挑战。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本章文档\">本章文档</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>文档</th>\n<th>主题</th>\n<th>核心概念</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"philosophy-of-computation\">计算哲学</a></td>\n<td>Church-Turing 论题的哲学边界</td>\n<td>超计算、物理主义、计算的内在性</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"information-dynamics\">信息动力学</a></td>\n<td>Barwise/Seligman 信道理论</td>\n<td>信息流、约束关系、情境语义</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"digital-ontology\">数字本体论</a></td>\n<td>信息结构主义</td>\n<td>it from bit、数字/模拟区分</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"章节定位\">章节定位</h2><p>计算哲学章节将前三章的理论推向本体论极限：如果信息是根本性的，那么计算和数字现实的地位是什么？这对程序员理解自己工作的深层含义有独特价值。</p>\n"}